  "basis": "The dashboard displays a dual-axis line chart for 'United States vs Canada'. The United States series (blue line, left axis) and Canada series (red line, right axis) have no visible numeric y-axis tick labels or scale calibration. At the 2013 x-axis position, the blue marker is visually lower on the page than the red marker. However, because the two y-axes are separate and lack visible numeric scales to establish a comparable magnitude, the vertical screen position alone is insufficient to determine which country had the larger application volume. The necessary condition for a public comparison (comparable scale) is not met by the visible evidence.",
